#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152040 :question/id #uuid "511feb42-d0dd-55b6-85c5-f0605fcf8da4" :question/math-academy-id "e-9454" :question/problem "A body of mass $3 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\textrm{N}).$\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) =t^2- e^{t-4}$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=4$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-{e}^{t-4}) \\\\  & =2t-{e}^{t-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=4 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =2(4)-{e}^{4-4} \\\\  & =8-1 \\\\  & =7\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =3\\cdot (7) \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F| = |21| = 21 \\, \\textrm{N}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152049 :question/id #uuid "3ecb82f0-3877-5732-851d-adec73abb890" :question/math-academy-id "e-9859" :question/problem "A body of mass $2 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t) = e^{3t-6} + t^2$ meters. Find the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t-6}+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t-6}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{e}^{3t-6}+2t) \\\\  & =9{e}^{3t-6}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force acting on the body, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =2\\cdot (9{e}^{3t-6}+2) \\\\  & =18{e}^{3t-6}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152050 :question/id #uuid "2666ce7a-356a-574a-88fd-97417afc8ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-9860" :question/problem "A body of mass $2 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ moves in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\geq 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) =2t^3-12t^2-30t+5$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time when the force acting on the body has a magnitude of zero." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}-30t+5) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-24t-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}-24t-30 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-4t-5 & =0 \\\\ (t+1)(t-5) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t \\geq 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude when $t=5 \\, \\textrm{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89ff05b3-8972-588d-ae6f-df0358b83777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149082} {:answer/id #uuid "922f7fcb-eccd-567f-b28a-fe340222674e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149083} {:answer/id #uuid "d79f0321-3bbb-5187-87cf-adab19f2dbf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149084} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e579d6-a04e-54e5-86ce-afa8fc7bca77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149085} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f167c5-4f9a-5967-8d5e-867e9bc9d4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149086}] :answer-field/id #uuid "da3d738c-967d-5ff7-896b-9fdd8c899b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149081}] :question/id #uuid "b8133d70-28c3-58c4-b2ef-3b4c9db4b987" :question/math-academy-id "q-138758" :question/problem "A body of mass $2kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons $(N)$.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) = 4t - 3t^{2}$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t = 2$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00994da2-e2d7-5f3a-afa1-c3f56a144ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t^{2} - 2e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149088} {:answer/id #uuid "11187e1f-b14a-53cf-9604-7e24d216b97d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30t - 10e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149089} {:answer/id #uuid "1a49c699-b063-5dc5-84b0-8608768fefdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15t^{2} - 10e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149090} {:answer/id #uuid "38523a3f-1ffa-5a8c-88d6-4c84b2113c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5t^{3} - 10e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149091} {:answer/id #uuid "404cc761-aee0-5953-a890-bdb4e9192040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{3} - 2e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149092}] :answer-field/id #uuid "812c9201-2a01-54a6-a98e-31d4741b35da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149087}] :question/id #uuid "a252b534-6672-5176-91ec-3c187772280e" :question/math-academy-id "q-138759" :question/problem "A body of mass $5kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) = t^{3} - 2e^{t}$ meters per second.\nFind an expression for the force acting on the body at time $t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95151cf7-7c09-569f-9d5c-36b9d082a067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - \\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149094} {:answer/id #uuid "36b97db8-c354-59e3-91ce-5a7b7487ff93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 + 4\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149095} {:answer/id #uuid "5a42509e-02b4-5238-a2b4-77254b3ec9f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - 4\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149096} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1ace99-9b07-5c0a-808b-067beabd896e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 + 8\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149097} {:answer/id #uuid "762e30c0-a68f-5acf-b298-8fed8bf6c947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + \\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149098}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1490c38c-4cdd-5be8-9d36-3091bcfdcf5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dae41bbd-829e-5684-b64d-8c75b12b2470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367458} {:answer/id #uuid "ab44549e-85bd-52d0-9191-de0ef0ee3087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367459} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ed92fd-dfc4-5696-ba8c-ebac3be43f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367460} {:answer/id #uuid "ba8f5dee-0941-5eb3-ad06-12456af906c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367461} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2b4e65-4960-5ac6-b252-6d556622c14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6ed92fd-dfc4-5696-ba8c-ebac3be43f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367460} :answer-field/id #uuid "df40aef9-2071-5dad-a80a-a6e73214fdbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e80cc7a9-739d-5325-ae21-392ab1ab7373" :question/math-academy-id "q-138760" :question/problem "A body of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2 \\\\  & =2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =8-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a212fe27-31f9-5c6e-9414-d256b2b7295d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149100} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bd68bc-250f-532d-8df6-bff34bf05ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149101} {:answer/id #uuid "03bae528-a1fb-5a54-81c5-86016f8f8fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149102} {:answer/id #uuid "31eab20c-fa66-5699-8a9c-d612ad3b8869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149103} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9ec473-72ab-593e-bc71-8c45d82e8ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149104}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a5c718-70a1-56d2-ba3a-e47d041c2343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149099}] :question/id #uuid "3f8838a5-79b1-5509-b773-12ce6251b077" :question/math-academy-id "q-138767" :question/problem "A body of mass $8kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons $(N)$.\nAt time $t > 0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t) = 2\\sqrt{t}$ meters.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t = 4$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec979ad-f34b-5bc2-82b8-6f41a068f0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266411} {:answer/id #uuid "48a8334b-0ef9-5191-9127-44e631521775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=6\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266794} {:answer/id #uuid "52dd010c-087d-5fb4-9015-5fb030abceef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=1\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266884} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea574e9-ed16-5575-a8f7-9e876cdae7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267115} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6df2d5-7b6e-56de-bfd2-16b3717e3350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e6df2d5-7b6e-56de-bfd2-16b3717e3350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267413} :answer-field/id #uuid "df5718bd-5b6c-5679-a0fe-b40c294fb6c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "396d3531-2c0c-5e02-bb04-58dd2fc7f372" :question/math-academy-id "q-138769" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}-36t+2$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}-36t+2) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-6t-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}-6t-36 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t-6 & =0 \\\\ (t-3)(t+2) & =0 \\\\ t & =-2,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "575bb501-1712-54b3-98a0-1cc23578739f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266922} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5badc5-4ac6-5f49-8bbb-f834296b0988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=4\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266952} {:answer/id #uuid "81a27545-523a-5abd-a925-1db42abf4ab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267285} {:answer/id #uuid "9f025b33-5d47-50b1-83db-fefb14a43c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267580} {:answer/id #uuid "d54698f9-e1d9-515a-8cef-385476f4d395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=7\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f025b33-5d47-50b1-83db-fefb14a43c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267580} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ee6c02-20b0-5395-ab50-9035b7c0dff6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8295ff34-59d6-595e-a3a0-97b1c540771c" :question/math-academy-id "q-138770" :question/problem "A body of mass $1.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+t-5$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+t-5) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-24t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-24t+1) \\\\  & =12t-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12t-24 & =0 \\\\ 12 & =24 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122c08d1-d87e-5c2d-b5fd-55849221e198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266296} {:answer/id #uuid "b0df363d-24c0-57cb-8740-440c49dc95b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡t-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267737} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf414aa-2630-5475-a5c0-66b83d890140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267850} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cf4c06-bbf0-5fcb-8f39-d44a90645423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268155} {:answer/id #uuid "f265a1cd-cc5d-5b68-ae41-46b1bda457d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡t-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf414aa-2630-5475-a5c0-66b83d890140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267850} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9f75a84-b0fb-513c-94dd-af85fccbabb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "03bfb990-1f26-5661-91b6-3c45e83b54ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-138881" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+2t$ meters per second.\nFind an expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+2t) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡t+2) \\\\  & =2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52e8f06f-e916-5347-a4c9-4dee21dbf354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9t-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266885} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2804c3-8dd8-58c6-9a21-51bdd234249e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{2}+4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267231} {:answer/id #uuid "8df9b3d5-5c50-5bcc-895e-09baf489d1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18t+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267408} {:answer/id #uuid "c494009d-1de7-5aa7-bb9f-fa6d26895270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{t}^{2}-12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267903} {:answer/id #uuid "c6677570-bf42-5a8a-8514-4e594503812c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-2t" :db/id #