{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,\\text{N}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266635} {:answer/id #uuid "ce953a5a-bdf1-5970-a0ac-7194863d8e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{N}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267990} {:answer/id #uuid "e0757d4b-04ec-5ade-9bed-ef0b3e4418ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{N}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27c0da78-93db-5949-b070-6f981810703d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,\\text{N}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266497} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce15ddde-aabd-5f3a-85cb-993bb216ff83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "02a00c93-382a-5e86-9629-662a2b661d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-138889" :question/problem "A body of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=4\\sqrt{t}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-3)$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=4$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}-\\frac{5}{t-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}}-\\frac{5}{4-3} \\\\  & =1-5 \\\\  & =-4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F|=|-32|=32\\,\\text{N}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13cbe687-e21f-5038-9eb2-b546590bf0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{t}^{2}-9t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266315} {:answer/id #uuid "2351970e-8c78-5618-b16d-c3be0143a643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24{t}^{2}-12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266467} {:answer/id #uuid "2be7459a-89f7-544d-b540-499c66147830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{2}+6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266533} {:answer/id #uuid "cb363477-24c1-58ae-b83a-0f77a554f579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{t}^{2}-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267962} {:answer/id #uuid "d901cb54-060e-50de-8644-0da99dbacfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16{t}^{2}+12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13cbe687-e21f-5038-9eb2-b546590bf0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{t}^{2}-9t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266315} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5fc313a-53f7-530d-9cca-87e0c50c8fd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9f7aa7b0-ac31-5117-9ffe-fef9bf62cd13" :question/math-academy-id "q-138900" :question/problem "A body of mass $1.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={t}^{4}-{t}^{3}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =1.5\\cdot (12{t}^{2}-6t) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-9t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22eac117-897c-5284-b6d8-d6070a0491ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24{e}^{2t}-12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266460} {:answer/id #uuid "390c0cb4-60f2-5e29-95b3-33fe5fa56990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{e}^{2t}-12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266640} {:answer/id #uuid "60d5bc7e-d2ab-5820-bed8-8e480e74facc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{2t}-6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267001} {:answer/id #uuid "7820a9b6-aefb-5331-b4d0-a36fd4eed302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{2t}-18t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267198} {:answer/id #uuid "edfa3b58-2e8e-5e5e-b2f5-2db37be9e31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2t}-6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7820a9b6-aefb-5331-b4d0-a36fd4eed302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{2t}-18t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267198} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1bbcf02-1f34-5745-9157-c049b449e68d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9e7d45cf-09f2-50ec-8c0d-cf33253cd459" :question/math-academy-id "q-138901" :question/problem "A body of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={e}^{2t}-{t}^{3}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{2t}-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{2t}-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =3\\cdot (4{e}^{2t}-6t) \\\\  & =12{e}^{2t}-18t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d74a74-5f32-5de1-9436-d960386a0a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{t\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266306} {:answer/id #uuid 